{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review political party compliance with Equality Act 2010",
        "additional_details": "Political parties play a key role in UK democracy and must obey equality laws. We believe that defining mainstream religious or ethnic identity components\u2014such as Jewish self-determination\u2014as inherently racist risks creating a hostile environment. In our view this also risks breaching Sections 13, 19, and 26 of the Equality Act 2010. We believe a review is needed to ensure that political parties comply with the Equality Act 2010 regarding religious and ethnic protections.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to review regulatory mechanisms for ensuring political parties\u2019 compliance with the Equality Act 2010 regarding religious and ethnic protections.",
